{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:eab42e86e73163d56943c2d3a1d64a26", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 13, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "backup.sh is done and syntax-checked:\n\n- `tar -czf logs-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz logs/` - bundles the log directory into a dated tarball (already present, kept as-is)\n- `scp \"$BUNDLE\" backup-srv:/srv/nightly/` - copies the tarball to the destination you gave\n- `set -eu` means the run aborts if the tarball or the copy fails, so tonight's cron run won't silently report a partial backup\n- `scp` and `tar` are both on this host\n\nOne dependency to know before tonight: `scp` to `backup-srv` assumes the job host can reach that name via `/etc/hosts` or DNS and has key-based (or otherwise non-interactive) auth set up to `backup-srv:/srv/nightly`. If either is missing the copy will fail - the script will exit non-zero, which is the safe failure mode.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:658ee0335cc6591a3f479c771bec20f6"}
